    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While I understand your concern, I'd strongly encourage against self-diagnosing your symptoms and using the medication on an ad hoc basis. Further, it's important to consider that symptoms of heart-related issues may also appear as transient chest discomfort, especially during physical activity. Over-reliance on Pepcid without medical oversight could mask a more serious underlying condition. Regularly experiencing these symptoms should prompt a consultation with a healthcare professional. Initially, simple management options can be useful, such as:\n1. Elevating the head during sleep to prevent nighttime symptoms.\n2. Avoiding eating right before bedtime or heavy meals.\n3. Limiting caffeine and acidic foods throughout the day.\n\nIf avoiding these items does not lead to relief, a tentative visit to a clinic, even if delayed to next month, is more prudent than the increased likelihood of exacerbating a potentially serious condition by delaying seeking professional advice. Remember, the earlier a health condition is detected and managed, the better the outcome is likely to be. Until you're able to schedule a professional appointment, observe any other symptoms, and try to rest well after meals. Immediate medical attention is needed if you experience increasing severity of symptoms, such as chest pain, difficulty breathing, or if the \"hot pressure\" feels like severe",
